  "notes": "{網羅|もうら} implies comprehensive, exhaustive coverage of a subject or collection.\n\nWRITING:\n- {網|もう} (net, mesh)\n- {羅|ら} (thin silk, gauze; to spread out)\n\nETYMOLOGY:\nThe word evokes the image of a net that catches everything - nothing escapes.\n\nUSAGE:\n- {網羅|もうら}する (to cover comprehensively - suru verb)\n- {網羅|もうら}{的|てき} (comprehensive, exhaustive - na-adjective)\n- {情報|じょうほう}を{網羅|もうら}する (to comprehensively cover information)\n- {全|ぜん}{項目|こうもく}を{網羅|もうら}する (to cover all items)\n- {網羅|もうら}{的|てき}なリスト (a comprehensive list)",
